+# Audit 0.15.0: night light, daylight nudge, wind-down
+
+Method: design review only (detector not applicable, native platform): impeccable (Android
+"dark theme is a first-class scheme", craft floor contrast) and graphic-design-fundamentals §13, on
+`today_night_light_sleeping`, `day_night_light_ptBR`, `today_daylight_nudge_light`.
+
+## graphic-design-fundamentals §13
+
+| # | Check | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Brief | Research-backed light features, Tatá's red/amber question answered. ✅ |
+| 2 | Concept | The phone becomes a warm night lamp. ✅ |
+| 3 | Hierarchy | Same structure; the amber action still leads. ✅ |
+| 4 | Contrast | Every pair passes in night (ink 9.3:1, muted 5.6:1, events ≥ 3:1 on page and on their rounds). ✅ |
+| 5 | Alignment | Unchanged. ✅ |
+| 6 | Spacing | Unchanged; the nudge is one row. ✅ |
+| 7 | Typography | Unchanged. ✅ |
+| 8 | Colour | Monochrome warm at night (60/30/10 holds: black, deep browns, amber accent); data told apart by lightness and always worded. ✅ |
+| 9 | Consistency | One theme switch; every component follows the roles. ✅ |
+| 10 | Simplicity | One setting; the nudge is one tap; the wind-down is one more phrase. ✅ |
+| 11 | Real size | Checked on phone screenshots, EN and PT. ✅ |
+| 12 | Accessibility | Contrast passes; no motion added. ✅ |
+| 13 | Production | Generated from tokens; a theme fallback so night lists only what changes. ✅ |
+
+Fixed in this release: the nudge's copy wrapped to three lines beside its button; shortened.
+Polish, kept: the header's brand mark stays teal at night (small, and the mark).
+
+## impeccable critique
+
+| # | Heuristic | Score | Note |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | System status | 4 | The theme changes with the clock, by itself. |
+| 2 | Real world | 4 | "Night light", "Go outside". |
+| 3 | Control | 4 | A switch for each. |
+| 4 | Consistency | 4 | Same layout in every theme. |
+| 5 | Error prevention | n/a | |
+| 6 | Recognition | 4 | Words beside every colour. |
+| 7 | Efficiency | 4 | Go outside starts the walk in one tap. |
+| 8 | Aesthetic | 4 | Warm, calm, cohesive. |
+| 9 | Error recovery | n/a | |
+| 10 | Help | 4 | The Settings line says the hours and why. |
+| | **Total** | **32/32** | |
